# Chat

A one-page chat room: `Publish`/`When a message arrives` delivers a message
to every page on the topic, including the sender's own — `docs/frontend.md`'s
Triggers ping example, extended to a real message log. A `## Store … shared
on` holds the other shared fact the room needs — how many visitors are here —
and `PresenceCount` shows it inside the page's own `View:`.

## Note

`## Store Presence shared on "chat-presence"` keeps `onlineCount` as a
`Tally`: every replica's joins and leaves add up, so two visitors arriving at
the same moment are both counted, where a plain field would keep whichever
write it saw last. The standalone test further down `Mount`s `PresenceCount`
on its own, the way `docs/frontend.md`'s "Testing a page" section tests a bare
`## Component` — and every test in this file starts with the page already
arrived: a `## Page` mounts itself before any test statement runs, so its
`When the page loads:` join is every test's prologue. `PresenceCount` mounted
on its own reads the shared store as the page's arrival left it, one visitor
counted. A file with no page is the tool for a topic nobody has touched.

## Store Presence shared on "chat-presence"

State:
    Let onlineCount: Tally be 0.

Actions:
    To join:
        Increase onlineCount by 1.

    To leave:
        Decrease onlineCount by 1.

## Component PresenceCount

Use Presence.

View:
    <span id="online">{Presence's onlineCount} online</span>

## Test: PresenceCount runs on its own, standalone

Mount PresenceCount.
Expect that the text of "#online" is equal to "1 online".

## Page /

Use Presence.

State:
    Let username be "ada".
    Let draft be "".
    Let pending be "".
    Let messages be a new Seq of Text.

Actions:
    When the page loads:
        Call Presence's join.

    To send:
        If draft is not equal to "":
            Set pending to username + ": " + draft.
            Publish pending on "chat-room".
            Set draft to "".

    When a message arrives on "chat-room" (m: Text):
        Push m to messages.

View:
    <main class="card">
      <header><h1>Chat room</h1><PresenceCount/></header>
      <ul id="log">
          {for each m in messages, at index i:}
              <li id="msg-{i}">{m}</li>
          {else:}
              <li class="empty">No messages yet.</li>
          {end}
      </ul>
      <form id="composer" on-submit.prevent={send}>
          <label for="draft">Message</label>
          <input id="draft" type="text" bind={draft} placeholder="Say something…">
          <button type="submit">Send</button>
      </form>
    </main>

## Test: an empty room shows its placeholder, one visitor present

Expect that the text of ".empty" is equal to "No messages yet.".
Expect that the text of "#online" is equal to "1 online".

## Test: sending a message delivers it back to the same page

Type "hello" into "#draft".
Submit "#composer".
Expect that the text of "#msg-1" is equal to "ada: hello".
Expect that the value of "#draft" is equal to "".

## Test: several messages keep their order

Type "first" into "#draft".
Submit "#composer".
Type "second" into "#draft".
Submit "#composer".
Expect that the count of "#log li" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#msg-1" is equal to "ada: first".
Expect that the text of "#msg-2" is equal to "ada: second".

## Test: an empty draft sends nothing

Submit "#composer".
Expect that the text of ".empty" is equal to "No messages yet.".
